# 1️⃣ Recover Binary Search Tree

## 📖 Problem

Sometimes two nodes of a BST are accidentally swapped.

Restore the BST without changing its structure.

Example:

```text
Correct BST:

        3
       / \
      1   4
         /
        2
```

Suppose two nodes are swapped.

The goal is to identify the incorrect nodes and swap their values back.

---

# 2️⃣ Important Observation

Inorder traversal of a valid BST is sorted.

Example:

```text
1 2 3 4 5
```

If two nodes are swapped:

```text
1 4 3 2 5
```

We can detect the positions where:

```text
previous > current
```

These violations help identify the swapped nodes.

---

### C++ Code

```cpp
class Solution
{
private:

    Node* first = NULL;
    Node* second = NULL;
    Node* prev = NULL;

    void inorder(Node* root)
    {
        if(root == NULL)
            return;

        inorder(root->left);

        if(prev != NULL &&
           prev->data > root->data)
        {
            if(first == NULL)
                first = prev;

            second = root;
        }

        prev = root;

        inorder(root->right);
    }

public:

    void recoverTree(Node* root)
    {
        inorder(root);

        if(first != NULL && second != NULL)
        {
            swap(first->data, second->data);
        }
    }
};
```

### Complexity

```text
Time: O(n)

Space: O(h)
```

