# 3️⃣ Two Sum in BST

## 📖 Problem

Given a BST and a target value `k`, determine whether there are two different nodes whose values add up to `k`.

Example:

```text
          5
        /   \
       3     6
      / \     \
     2   4     7
```

Target:

```text
9
```

Possible pair:

```text
2 + 7 = 9
```

Answer:

```text
true
```

---

# 4️⃣ Approach 1: Inorder + Two Pointers

Inorder traversal gives sorted values.

```text
2 3 4 5 6 7
```

Then use two pointers:

```text
left → beginning

right → end
```

If:

```text
sum < target
```

Move:

```text
left++
```

If:

```text
sum > target
```

Move:

```text
right--
```

---

### C++ Code

```cpp
bool twoSumBST(Node* root, int target)
{
    vector<int> values;

    inorder(root, values);

    int left = 0;
    int right = values.size() - 1;

    while(left < right)
    {
        int sum = values[left] + values[right];

        if(sum == target)
            return true;

        if(sum < target)
            left++;
        else
            right--;
    }

    return false;
}
```

### Complexity

```text
Time: O(n)

Space: O(n)
```

