# 🔟 Balance a BST

## 📖 Problem

Given an unbalanced BST, convert it into a balanced BST.

Example:

```text
Unbalanced:

1
 \
  2
   \
    3
     \
      4
```

Convert to:

```text
        2
       / \
      1   3
           \
            4
```

---

# 1️⃣1️⃣ Approach

### Step 1

Perform inorder traversal.

This produces a sorted array:

```text
1 2 3 4
```

### Step 2

Build a balanced BST from the sorted array.

Use the middle element as the root.

---

### C++ Code

```cpp
void storeInorder(
    Node* root,
    vector<int>& values)
{
    if(root == NULL)
        return;

    storeInorder(root->left, values);

    values.push_back(root->data);

    storeInorder(root->right, values);
}

Node* buildBalanced(
    vector<int>& values,
    int left,
    int right)
{
    if(left > right)
        return NULL;

    int mid =
        left + (right - left) / 2;

    Node* root =
        new Node(values[mid]);

    root->left =
        buildBalanced(
            values,
            left,
            mid - 1
        );

    root->right =
        buildBalanced(
            values,
            mid + 1,
            right
        );

    return root;
}

Node* balanceBST(Node* root)
{
    vector<int> values;

    storeInorder(root, values);

    return buildBalanced(
        values,
        0,
        values.size() - 1
    );
}
```

### Complexity

```text
Time: O(n)

Space: O(n)
```

