# 1️⃣2️⃣ Merge Two BSTs

## 📖 Problem

Given two BSTs, create a sorted list containing all their elements.

Example:

```text
BST 1:

    2
   / \
  1   4
```

```text
BST 2:

    3
   / \
  0   5
```

Merged result:

```text
0 1 2 3 4 5
```

---

# 1️⃣3️⃣ Approach

Since inorder traversal of a BST gives sorted values:

```text
BST 1 → Sorted Array

BST 2 → Sorted Array
```

Then merge the two sorted arrays.

---

### C++ Code

```cpp
void inorder(
    Node* root,
    vector<int>& values)
{
    if(root == NULL)
        return;

    inorder(root->left, values);

    values.push_back(root->data);

    inorder(root->right, values);
}

vector<int> mergeBSTs(
    Node* root1,
    Node* root2)
{
    vector<int> a;
    vector<int> b;

    inorder(root1, a);
    inorder(root2, b);

    vector<int> result;

    int i = 0;
    int j = 0;

    while(i < a.size() &&
          j < b.size())
    {
        if(a[i] < b[j])
            result.push_back(a[i++]);
        else
            result.push_back(b[j++]);
    }

    while(i < a.size())
        result.push_back(a[i++]);

    while(j < b.size())
        result.push_back(b[j++]);

    return result;
}
```

### Complexity

```text
Time: O(n + m)

Space: O(n + m)
```

