# 1️⃣4️⃣ Largest BST in a Binary Tree

## 📖 Problem

Given a Binary Tree, find the size of the largest subtree that is also a valid BST.

Example:

```text
          10
         /  \
        5    15
       / \     \
      1   8     7
```

The subtree rooted at `5` is a valid BST:

```text
      5
     / \
    1   8
```

Size:

```text
3
```

---

# 1️⃣5️⃣ Information Required

For every subtree, we need:

```text
Minimum Value

Maximum Value

Size

Is BST?
```

Then determine whether the current subtree is a BST.

---

### C++ Structure

```cpp
struct Info
{
    int minimum;
    int maximum;
    int size;
    bool isBST;
};
```

---

### C++ Code

```cpp
Info solve(Node* root, int& answer)
{
    if(root == NULL)
    {
        return {
            INT_MAX,
            INT_MIN,
            0,
            true
        };
    }

    Info left = solve(root->left, answer);

    Info right = solve(root->right, answer);

    Info current;

    current.size =
        left.size + right.size + 1;

    if(left.isBST &&
       right.isBST &&
       left.maximum < root->data &&
       root->data < right.minimum)
    {
        current.isBST = true;

        current.minimum =
            min(root->data, left.minimum);

        current.maximum =
            max(root->data, right.maximum);

        answer =
            max(answer, current.size);
    }
    else
    {
        current.isBST = false;

        current.minimum = INT_MIN;
        current.maximum = INT_MAX;
    }

    return current;
}
```

### Complexity

```text
Time: O(n)

Space: O(h)
```

