# 💡 Interview Tips

✅ Remember that inorder traversal of a BST is sorted.

✅ Use reverse inorder for descending order.

✅ BST Iterator is basically controlled inorder traversal.

✅ To balance a BST, convert it to a sorted sequence and rebuild it using middle elements.

✅ For complex subtree problems, return multiple pieces of information from recursion.

✅ Always consider whether the BST property can eliminate unnecessary traversal.

---

# ⚠️ Common Mistakes

❌ Forgetting to check both left and right subtree conditions.

❌ Using an unordered traversal when sorted order is required.

❌ Forgetting that duplicate handling depends on the BST definition.

❌ Creating an unnecessarily skewed tree from a sorted array.

❌ Confusing BST Iterator with a normal Binary Tree traversal.

❌ Forgetting that a subtree must satisfy the BST property at every level.

